      "writtenOn": "2024-05-28T22:28:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Last I checked, checkpatch tries to identify commit SHAs as ancestor commits. So if `aaef73821a3b` is not an ancestor of this commit, this check will fail. And indeed, `aaef73821a3b` is not an ancestor of android14-6.1. This check makes more sense for `Fixes: aaef73821a3b(...)`, I guess and is otherwise an instance of checkpatch not working well on linux-mainline.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "097984c5c4e27c111a5c411cee8bc60ad3576e47",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f512b0ba_1530c75e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1402878
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-28T22:30:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To be clear: A person reading _this_ commit message is not guaranteed to have `aaef73821a3b` available even with full history of _this_ commit. And that is why this check fails.",
      "parentUuid": "353c08ca_2aae9276",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 61
